<p>In the latest development, Israel and Lebanon agreed in Washington to extend their U.S.-mediated ceasefire by three weeks after meetings involving representatives from both countries and President Trump. The extension gives both sides another chance to avoid a return to full-scale war along the Israel-Lebanon border, though the truce remains fragile as fighting has intensified in recent days. Even with the extension, clashes and strikes continued in southern Lebanon. Al Jazeera reported that Israeli forces killed six Hezbollah fighters in an exchange of fire near Bint Jbeil, while other coverage said both Israel and Hezbollah have committed multiple violations since the ceasefire began, testing whether the arrangement can hold. Reports from Beirut also described concern that Israel is using the ceasefire period to shape new security realities in southern Lebanon, underscoring how diplomacy and battlefield developments are unfolding at the same time.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TAToAClco4v3AcZDHGZnwmr5xEaH_EGRnQma7WsARiUNB_qiOVv1dBqaGNJgTWzCfE4ykNo7BmayC0G2ktQ9LvlpUk99yScOSPKpCMKu8FDEKArfZpCsqdPZ6TDAEC1ZaZFYJjklp_lLLEpyYNLFMnS8N_viFp-LjGZVEoq4_nwcHwA2Bittd4N2xKUs25zMyP25GKSfQSWfJgMDfiC4OluRzhth7-ZRf2E' alt='A disabled ambulance sat amid rubble from an Israeli strike on Nabatieh, Lebanon, earlier this week. Strikes by both Israel and Hezbollah diminished since a cease-fire began last week, but clashes have intensified in recent days.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ground damage: The New York Times described a disabled ambulance sitting amid rubble from an Israeli strike on Nabatieh, a stark reminder that civilian infrastructure in southern Lebanon remains exposed even with the truce formally in place.</li><li>Local losses: PBS reported that communities in southern Lebanon are still assessing damage from Israeli strikes as the ceasefire hangs by a thread, showing that reconstruction needs are growing even before a stable calm has taken hold.</li><li>Border tension: The New York Times said the ceasefire had stopped an all-out war between Israel and Hezbollah, but intensifying attacks by both sides are now putting that restraint under renewed pressure.</li><li>Security debate: RT reported allegations from Beirut that Israel is using the extension period to impose a &#x27;Gaza-style yellow zone&#x27; in southern Lebanon, highlighting a disputed question over how the border area will be controlled if the truce survives.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: President Trump announced the three-week extension after meeting representatives from Israel and Lebanon in Washington, framing it as the latest U.S. effort to keep the border truce alive. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-hezbollah-ceasefire-extended-by-3-weeks-says-trump/article70899310.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Israel: Israeli forces continued military action after the extension. Al Jazeera reported that they killed six Hezbollah fighters near Bint Jbeil during an exchange of fire, indicating that Israel still sees active threats on the ground. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/24/israel-continues-attacks-on-lebanon-despite-extension-of-ceasefire'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: Coverage from PBS and The New York Times said Hezbollah has also been accused of violating the ceasefire, showing that the group remains part of the escalation cycle threatening the truce. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/southern-lebanon-weighs-losses-from-israeli-strikes-as-ceasefire-hangs-by-a-thread'>PBS NewsHour</a>, <a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/24/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-fighting-ceasefire.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Beirut-based critics: RT&#x27;s report from Beirut said critics believe Israel is using the ceasefire period to create a new controlled zone in southern Lebanon, reflecting concern in Lebanon that temporary calm could reshape facts on the ground. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639032-israel-lebanon-ceasefire-extension/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-hezbollah-ceasefire-extended-by-3-weeks-says-trump/article70899310.ece'>Israel-Lebanon ceasefire extended by three weeks</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639032-israel-lebanon-ceasefire-extension/'>Israel using ceasefire to impose ‘Gaza‑style yellow zone’ in south Lebanon</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/24/israel-continues-attacks-on-lebanon-despite-extension-of-ceasefire'>Israel continues attacks on Lebanon despite extension of ceasefire</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/24/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-fighting-ceasefire.html'>Israel-Lebanon Cease-Fire Tested by Escalating Clashes</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/southern-lebanon-weighs-losses-from-israeli-strikes-as-ceasefire-hangs-by-a-thread'>Southern Lebanon weighs losses from Israeli strikes as ceasefire hangs by a thread</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>